# CODEOWNERS — Maintainer governance (inspired by openai/codex)
# https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Rule: patterns later in the file take precedence (last match wins).
#       Hence the catch-all * is at the top, specific paths below.
# With branch protection (require_code_owner_reviews):
#   a PR touching a path must be approved by its owner before merging.
#
# Roles:
#   maintainer = @JackyChen-China   (final merge decision on source code)
#   committer  = @ai007-explorer org (governance / CI / docs approval)
#   .github governance also requires @trublion1116
# Source changes need maintainer approval; governance/CI/docs changes need
# at least one committer.

# ── Default catch-all (anything not matched above → whole org) ───────────
*                                           @ai007-explorer

# ── Core source (maintainer only) ────────────────────────────────────────
/server.js                                   @JackyChen-China
/auth.js                                     @JackyChen-China
/projection-route.js                         @JackyChen-China
/gen_projection.py                           @JackyChen-China
/public/                                     @JackyChen-China

# ── Governance / CI / merge mechanism (changes need broader visibility) ──
# A single /.github/ rule covers every file under .github/ (CODEOWNERS,
# settings.yml, workflows/, scripts/). CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so
# listing specific files above a directory rule would be overridden anyway.
/.github/                                   @ai007-explorer @JackyChen-China @trublion1116

# ── Docs / deployment config ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/README.md                                  @ai007-explorer @JackyChen-China
/railway.json                               @ai007-explorer @JackyChen-China
/projection.json                            @ai007-explorer @JackyChen-China
